{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479045-how-to-make-a-gunsmith-character","id":1479045,"title":"How to make a gunsmith character?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-17T18:31:54-07:00","id":1479045,"title":"How to make a gunsmith character?","content":"So one of my players in my Origin game is making a character who is a gunsmith, but she is having problems figuring out her Role path skills since Scion's crafting for mundane items is not supremely well defined even with two books, since they seem to have completely dropped skills that could be used for craft-focused characters. What would people recommend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-17T18:39:40-07:00","id":1479046,"title":"","content":"I would have them craft guns with Firearms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T02:29:50-07:00","id":1479068,"title":"","content":"I think an important distinction to make here:<br /> <br /> Are they making a character that happen to be a gunsmith, or are they making a character where smithing is going to be part of their Legend in a significant fashion.<br /> <br /> If the gunsmithing is mostly early flavor, the previous suggestion of just using Firearms is plenty. &quot;I can make a basic gun,&quot; or, &quot;I can modify a gun to have some extra bits,&quot; probably aren't even worth rolling most of the time, or getting into the full Procedural Crafting rules.<br /> <br /> If the gunsmithing is going to get ramped up to divine levels, they're probably going to want to get the most out of complex actions with multiple milestones that require different dice pools. It's also going to be important to remember how the character approaches these things. Designing a gun and gathering parts is going to be very different for a character that's more focused on harvesting wood from a sacred tree for the stock (Survival/Occult) vs one that's custom making parts themselves with a full suite of modern tools (Technology/Science). Other skills might come in, in a number of ways as the PC might try to balance various considerations: Academics to cover knowing the legal process for registering a self-made gun or if the gun in question is even legal to make/own where they are, Persuasion or Subterfuge if they need a part or a form that's not easily obtained (or at least not without a lot of questions), etc.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T04:24:02-07:00","id":1479071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller323</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1479045-how-to-make-a-gunsmith-character#post1479045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So one of my players in my Origin game is making a character who is a gunsmith, but she is having problems figuring out her Role path skills since Scion's crafting for mundane items is not supremely well defined even with two books, since they seem to have completely dropped skills that could be used for craft-focused characters. What would people recommend?</div> </div> </div> </div>Crafting skill is Technology, if you want to make a character that create things using technical knowledge and building tools you use Technology. We can argue about it, but in the end, taking a compact list of skills is very positive to the flow of the game and character creation.<br /> <br /> Scion is not focused in the mundane part of the character life, so if you build buildings, cars or guns it\u2019s not relevant, as a god of creativity/construction/crafts usually is capable of constructing any of those with the same skill (it may take different amounts of time and materials, but they can build any of them). Your character is so capable, even as a Hero (or in Origin level) they can build basically any kind of mundane equipment as easy as if buying it, and the results would be good enough for most of the tables. To be fair, anything you want your character to have other than relics is just a matter of talking to the Storyguide.<br /> <br /> A character with a Gunsmith role would have Firearms and Technology skills at least. I would say Academics could be an option for a more traditionalist inventor, or Culture for a more modern style crafter (creating guns with a specific style, like anime guns, or old west guns, or ancient China hand cannons, or what ever). Would you use the skills during the game? Probably not. I would say a character with this path would have access to a huge number of guns, with any combination of tags, as long they can pop in their workshop to change the gun being used (be it to pick one that was ready or to build a new one).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T14:06:04-07:00","id":1479096,"title":"","content":"While Technology is an easy default, it's worth remembering that a lot of skills explicitly include basic maintenance of the tools of their trade as part of their operation without needing to extend to other skills. Most gunsmiths are not inventing new guns, but rather they have the time, experience, tools, and parts to do lots of jobs that most firearms users could do, but it's cheaper and faster to pay an expert to do. If you have the skills to take apart a gun to give it a full cleaning (again, something Firearms already covers), you have the skills to buy a skeleton trigger (skeleton parts are mostly to cut down on weight for competition weapons) kit and swap it out while adjusting the trigger pull to be bit more to your liking. But most competitive shooters just send their guns to a smith that does a full personalized rebuild. The smith has the parts, knows the different guns, probably has a testing range for QA, and so on.<br /> <br /> Technology is really only going to come up if you character designs custom parts. You don't need Technology to buy a new mouse for your computer, and you don't need it to swap one off-the-shelf sight for a different one (esp. on a modern gun with a rail system). I would stress Academics again, because it covers legal matters, and in huge swaths of the world gun laws are fairly complicated (and worse can change drastically even when traveling through otherwise simple borders). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T14:21:02-07:00","id":1479097,"title":"","content":"Agree completely. Technology would be for a smith that is creating the pieces and inventing new guns. Most of the maintenance, including changing parts, oiling and disassembly and assembly it back is a Firearms use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}